# Decisions log — fieldops-ui

`docs/decisions.md` is the review artifact. Commit bodies may point at it; they do not replace it.

Law: `.cursor/rules/030-decisions.mdc`. Shape: four fixed sections below. Micro-format inside defend/cut entries uses Why / What / Rejected / How.

## When to write

Same turn as the choice. Do not defer to handoff.

| Event | Section |
| --- | --- |
| Non-trivial library trade-off you would defend in review | §1 Five decisions to defend |
| Preset, peers, prepare, NativeWind/Tailwind wiring across package boundary | §2 NativeWind across package boundary |
| Deliberate non-build (scope cut, skipped approach, deferred feature) | §3 What we cut |
| First use of an AI tool in a work stream | §4 AI tools used and where |

Task that encodes a trade-off is incomplete until the matching section is updated.

## §1 — Five decisions to defend

Keep **exactly five** entries at handoff. Overflow goes under `### Candidates (prune before handoff)`, then merge or drop.

Each final entry:

```markdown
### <short title>
- **Why:** problem or constraint
- **What:** option chosen
- **Rejected:** option not taken, and why rejected
- **How:** paths, ports, package exports, commands
```

Typical defend topics: className merge, composable escape hatch, Select long-list, styling integrations port, builder-bob/peer/entry shape.

## §2 — NativeWind across package boundary

One narrative. Fill when styling crosses the package boundary. Required fields:

- **Problem:** what breaks if styles stay source-only or host is miswired
- **Solution:** what shipped (preset export, peers, prepare, integrations port, consumer steps)
- **Cost:** concrete trade-offs (setup burden, peer pins, dual build, DX friction)

Do not close preset/peer/NativeWind work with this section empty.

## §3 — What we cut (highest bar)

This section matters more than the others. Vague “kept scope small” fails.

Each cut:

```markdown
- **Cut:** specific thing not built
- **Why:** reason
- **Rejected alternative:** what was almost built instead
```

Good: “No dark mode.” “No sixth component.” “Select uses FlatList only after plain map proved insufficient — cut FlashList.”  
Bad: “Avoided overengineering.”

## §4 — AI tools used and where

Append on first use of that tool in a work stream. No per-prompt spam.

```markdown
- **Tool:** name (e.g. Cursor Agent, Claude)
- **Where:** what it touched (scaffold, spike, tests, docs)
- **Not used for:** optional honesty
```

## Must not

- Invent a sixth public component only to have something to log.
- Log chat fluff or process noise as decisions.
- Leave `<!-- replace -->` stubs in `docs/decisions.md` at handoff.
- Treat Why/What/How dated dump as the whole file — four grader sections are mandatory.
